WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:37.410
An entire summer was spent with Diana,
until one certain day.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.090
Well, well. She's finally back?

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.710
She is half an hour late.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:06.410
Matthew!

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.420
Anne!

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.070
I'm back, Matthew!

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.210
Matthew, I have a favor to ask of you.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.360
It's about Idlewild!

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.410
Mrs. Barry daughter and I...

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.870
made a house in Idlewild.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.010
We have a stove and chairs in there.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.370
But something's missing.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:40.190
Well now, it's a table, isn't it, Anne?

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:42.490
How did you know, Matthew?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.770
Well now, I just feel like
that's what is lacking.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.120
All right! I'll use the rest of the
wood to make you a table.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.620
Thank you, Matthew!

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.550
I'm sorry!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.870
How long will she talk there now that
she is half an hour late?

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:27.150
Matthew too, listening
to her like a perfect ninny.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.180
Anne, Anne!

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:30.940
Coming!

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.550
I'm back!

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:48.590
Oh, Marilla, there's going to be a
Sunday-school picnic next week

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:52.580
in Mr. Harmon Andrews's field, right
near the lake of Shining Waters.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:58.800
And Mrs. Superintendent Bell and Mrs.
Lynde are going to make ice cream!

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.540
Think of it, Marilla. Ice cream!

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.890
Oh, Marilla, can I go to it?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.910
Just look at the clock, if you please!

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.530
What time did I tell you to come in?

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:18.910
Two o'clock.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.410
But isn't it splendid about
the picnic, Marilla?

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.820
Please, can I go?

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.690
I've never been to a picnic.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:30.120
I've dreamed of picnics, but I've never...

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:35.810
I told you to come at two o'clock.
And it's a quarter to three.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.830
I'd like to know why you didn't obey me.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.120
Why, I meant to, as much as could be.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.680
But you have no idea
how fascinating Idlewild is.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.150
I don't want to know!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:55.380
And then, of course, I had to tell
Matthew about the picnic.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.770
Matthew is such a sympathetic listener.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.320
I can go, can't I?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.260
You'll have to learn to resist the fascination
of Idle-whatever-you-call-it.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:09.770
When I tell you to come in at a
certain time, I mean that time

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.780
and not half an hour later.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.810
And you needn't stop to discourse with
sympathetic listeners on your way, either.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.000
As for the picnic, of course you can go.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.420
You're a Sunday-school scholar,

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.960
and it's not likely I'd refuse to let you go
when all the other little girls are going.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.290
Thank you, Marilla!

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.340
But... but...

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:41.240
Diana says that everybody must
take a basket of things to eat.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:44.570
I can't cook, as you know...

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:50.860
and... and... I don't mind going to a
picnic without puffed sleeves so much,

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.810
but I'd feel terribly humiliated if
I had to go without a basket.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:58.370
It's been preying on my mind
ever since Diana told me.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:05.510
Well, it needn't prey any longer.
I'll bake you a basket.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.360
Oh, you dear good Marilla!
Oh, you are so kind to me!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.590
Oh, I'm so much obliged to you!

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.540
Oh, thank you, Marilla!

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.610
A-all right, t-that's enough.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:21.080
Anne, don't do that.
It's dangerous!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.720
There, there, never mind
your kissing nonsense.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.820
I'd sooner see you
doing strictly as you're told.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:34.560
As for cooking, I mean to
begin giving you lessons.

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.260
But you're so featherbrained,

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:42.040
I've been waiting to see if you'd sober down
a little and learn to be steady before I begin.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.790
You've got to keep your wits about
you in cooking and not stop in

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:48.810
the middle of things to let your
thoughts rove all over creation.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:54.090
Now, get out your patchwork and have
your square done before teatime.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:58.710
I do not like patchwork.
Because there's no scope for imagination in...

00:06:58.710 --> 00:06:59.530
Anne!

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:13.680
Diana is having a new dress
made with elbow sleeves.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.400
She is going to wear it to the picnic.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.680
Oh, I do hope it will be fine next Wednesday.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:22.320
I couldn't endure the disappointment
if anything happened

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.000
to prevent me from getting to the picnic.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:30.150
I suppose I'd live through it, but I'm
certain it would be a lifelong sorrow.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:34.490
It wouldn't matter if I got to
a hundred picnics in after years.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:39.250
They wouldn't make up for missing this one.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.500
They're going to have boats
on the Lake of Shining Waters.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.930
And ice cream!

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.710
Ice cream!

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:50.250
I have never tasted ice cream.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:54.260
Diana tried to explain what it was like,

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:58.040
but I guess ice cream is one of those
things that are beyond imagination.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:58.740
Anne!

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.450
You have talked even on
for ten minutes by the clock.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.830
Now, just for curiosity's sake,

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.820
see if you can hold your tongue
for the same length of time.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:39.020
Anne, it's still four days to the picnic.

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:41.010
Don't stand there staring outside all day.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.160
Anne Shirley, are you listening to me?

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:55.930
Now, I'm going to give you an
exciting announcement today.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.070
Although you must have heard of it,

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:04.030
we are organizing a picnic this Wednesday.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.970
Quiet, quiet!

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:13.160
Because the summer is ending soon,

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.600
I hope everyone will have fun on this picnic.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.600
When the minister announced the picnic,

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.030
such a thrill as went up and
down my back, Marilla!

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:40.910
Didn't you know last week
about the picnic already?

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:44.910
I don't think I'd ever
really believed until then

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:48.550
that there was honestly going to be a picnic.

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:51.140
I couldn't help fearing I'd only imagined it.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:55.260
But when a minister says a thing in
the pulpit you just have to believe it.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.590
You set your heart too
much on things, Anne.

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:02.810
There'll be a great many disappointments
in store for you through life.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:07.630
Oh, looking forward to things
is half the pleasure of them.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:10.790
You mayn't get the things themselves,

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.310
but nothing can prevent you from having
the fun of looking forward to them.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.670
That brooch was shining just now!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.830
It's a perfectly elegant brooch!

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:28.830
I don't know how you
can pay attention to the

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:31.210
sermon or the prayers
when you have it on.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.660
I couldn't, I know.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.850
I think amethysts are just sweet.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:42.340
They are what I used
to think diamonds were like.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:45.770
Long ago, before I had
ever seen a diamond,

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:49.430
I read about them and I tried to
imagine what they would be like.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:53.640
I thought they would be lovely
glimmering purple stones.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:58.630
When I saw a real diamond
in a lady's ring one day

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.280
I was so disappointed I cried.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:05.040
Of course, it was very lovely...

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:08.820
but it wasn't my idea of a diamond.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:31.720
I'm going to the Aid Society now.
Place the box upstairs.

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:32.770
All right!

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:32.560
How beautiful!

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:37.110
Amethysts must be the
souls of good violets.

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:53.180
Anne, did you see anything
of my amethyst brooch?

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:59.230
I thought I stuck it in my pincushion when
I came home from church yesterday,

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.180
but I can't find it anywhere.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:06.510
I saw it this afternoon when you
were away at the Aid Society.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:12.470
I was passing your door when
I saw it on the cushion,

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.660
so I went in to look at it.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.950
Did you touch it?

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:16.890
Yes.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:22.860
I took it up and I pinned it on my breast
just to see how it would look.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.670
You had no business to
do anything of the sort.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.830
It's very wrong in a little girl to meddle.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.490
You shouldn't have gone into
my room in the first place,

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:36.660
and you shouldn't have touched a brooch
that didn't belong to you in the second.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.990
Where did you put it?

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:43.560
Oh, I put it back on the bureau.
I hadn't it on a minute.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.870
Truly, I didn't mean to meddle.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:54.240
I didn't think about its being wrong to
go in and try on the brooch.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:58.320
But I see now that it was
and I'll never do it again.

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:03.260
That's one good thing about me.
I never do the same naughty thing twice.

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:07.710
You didn't put it back.
That brooch isn't anywhere on the bureau.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:11.010
You've taken it out or something, Anne.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.000
I did put it back.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:17.860
I don't just remember whether I stuck it on
the pincushion or laid it in the china tray.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.710
But I'm perfectly certain I put it back.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.450
I'll go and have another look.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:29.260
If you put that brooch back it's there still.
If it isn't I'll know you didn't, that's all!

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:30.030
Anne, the brooch is gone.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:35.660
By your own admission you were
the last person to handle it.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:40.450
Now, what have you done with it?
Tell me the truth at once.

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:42.380
Did you take it out and lose it?

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:44.170
No, I didn't.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:49.280
I never took the brooch out of your
room and that is the truth.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.730
If I was to be led to the block for it.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:56.930
Although I'm not very
certain what a block is.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.600
So there, Marilla.

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:02.920
I believe you are telling me a falsehood, Anne!

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:05.280
I know you are.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:11.150
There now, don't say anything more unless
you are prepared to tell the whole truth.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:15.830
Go to your room and stay there
until you are ready to confess.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.430
Will I take the peas with me?

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.820
No, I'll finish shelling them myself.

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.320
How didn't I know this would happen?

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:07.840
Of course, I don't suppose she meant
to steal it or anything like that.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:13.230
She's just taken it to play with or
help along that imagination of hers.

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:18.620
I suppose she has lost it and is afraid to
own up for fear she'll be punished.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:22.800
It's a dreadful thing to
think she tells falsehoods.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.870
It's a far worse thing than her fit of temper.

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:31.800
It's a fearful responsibility to have a
child in your house you can't trust.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.960
Slyness and untruthfulness.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:38.030
I declare I feel worse about that
than about the brooch.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:45.200
If she'd only have told the
truth about it I wouldn't mind so much.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:57.100
Marilla went to her room at intervals all
through the evening and searched for

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.390
the brooch, without finding it.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:22.090
I can't believe that child
would do something like that.

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:26.000
You're sure it hasn't fell down
behind the bureau?

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.100
I've moved the bureau and
I've taken out the drawers

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.550
and I've looked in every crack and cranny.

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:38.640
The brooch is gone and that child
has taken it and lied about it.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:41.630
We might as well look it in the face.

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:46.390
Well now, what are you going to do about it?

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.420
She'll stay in her room until she confesses.

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:51.920
It worked the last time.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.980
Is that so?

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.390
Then we'll see.

00:19:56.720 --> 00:20:01.980
Perhaps we'll be able to find the brooch
if she'll only tell where she took it.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:05.620
But in any case she'll have to be
severely punished, Matthew.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:11.040
Well now, you'll have to punish her.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.490
I've nothing to do with it, remember.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:18.310
You warned me off yourself.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:26.220
Marilla felt deserted by everyone.

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:34.310
It was daybreak, and Green Gables
in August was as beautiful as ever.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.120
Oh, Marilla, good morning.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:45.780
It's a beautiful day!

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:49.260
I hope tomorrow's picnic
will be as fine as today.

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:53.070
Haven't you found your brooch yet?

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.570
Didn't you lost it while taking it out, Anne?
Tell the truth at once!

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:57.900
I didn't take it!

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:40.580
Whenever it was mealtime, Marilla went up
to Anne's room with a very serious face,

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:44.340
and left it with a face more serious still.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.670
Anne steadfastly refused to confess.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:22:01.490
Marilla wanted to hear Mrs. Lynde's opinion,

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:05.850
but she had no courage due to
the seriousness of the matter.

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:25.620
And by night Marilla was tired.

00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:36.570
Although every time Marilla saw Anne's
crying face, she felt a pang of pity

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:40.040
which she sternly repressed.

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:43.940
How long will you stay like this, Anne?

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:54.760
I always though frankness
was your best quality.

00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:59.400
But... but how could I confess
about something I never did?

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:03.110
I didn't take it.

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:04.360
I really didn't.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:07.620
Oh, Marilla the picnic is tomorrow.

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:11.830
You won't keep me
from going to that, will you?

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:16.300
You'll just let me out for the afternoon,
won't you?

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:20.880
Then I'll stay here as long as you
like AFTERWARDS cheerfully.

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:23.850
But I MUST go to the picnic.

00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:28.340
You'll not go to picnics nor anywhere
else until you've confessed, Anne.

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:30.830
Oh, Marilla!

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:23.380
On the morning of the picnic day,
Anne finally determined herself.

00:24:24.260 --> 00:24:27.010
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:27.580 --> 00:24:29.610
Anne's Confession

00:24:29.610 --> 00:24:30.860
Please watch!
